WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.670
In July 2008, official inflation
in Zimbabwe reached 231

2
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.890
million per cent a year.

3
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:14.710
In January 2009, a single banknote was
issued for 100 trillion Zimbabwe dollars.

4
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:18.870
Its central bank had been creating
money to pay for government spending.

5
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.090
So if a country printed
twice as much money,

6
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.820
would everything really
cost twice as much?

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.980
In this mission, you'll meet
one equation that links money,

8
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.910
spending and prices.

9
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.370
Then you'll double the
money supply yourself,

10
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.880
and track output and the price level.

11
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.550
Your mission: find out when more
money really means higher prices.
